{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>So long as all the days of the earth.</b> This expression indicates that the world has a limit, a fixed time. And even though it is written deficient without a vav — for thus is its scriptural form, עד written thus, which would include the opposite (i.e., 'until' implying termination) — the reading is primary. זרע וקציר, 'seedtime and harvest': these are born and these die, and by means of what? By means of קור וחום, 'cold and heat.' And the sense of the verse will explain six matters which are the orders of the world, which do not cease by day and by night."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:17.929794886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}